    "observed_invariants": [
      "Filesystem admission precedes worker slot FIFO and CPU reservations; blocked filesystem waiters do not occupy the slot FIFO.",
      "Only actual helper execution holds candidate I/O lease; nested pre/post digest workers run outside it.",
      "Cancellation propagates through the worker private admission token; active jobs and held candidate FDs settle before their containing operation returns.",
      "Fresh candidate fstat rejects nonregular inputs promptly. Owned flag is allocated before open, cleared before close; outer synchronous ownership guard covers first closure/continuation allocation.",
      "Existing worker cancellation/CPUwait/apply/shutdown tests now use the I/O-enabled constructor and assert retained/settled I/O state.",
      "Endpoint-local registration uses the actual shared Prefs omission/incoming-isolation mechanism and actual runtime test confirms observed configuration."
    ],
    "limits": [
      "Untransferred worker duplicate FDs close immediately after I/O admission releases, on the same owner continuation before deferred dispatch; no worker is borrowing them. Documentation describes execution/completion rather than claiming a global FD ceiling.",
      "Ephemeral filesystem keys do not establish physical disk identity, mount incarnation, hostile path isolation, RSS or descriptor limits.",
      "Source review plus synthetic runtime fixtures is not SDK/Photo/native-validation or storage-throughput qualification."
    ]
  },
